    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.deps\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nmini.deps does not comprehensively scrub the environment before shelling out to `git`, causing git index corruption.\n\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/561751e839b99a4baca36b9d963166b66d2536a6/lua/mini/deps.lua#L1504-L1509\n\nthe lines above remove `GIT_DIR` and `GIT_WORK_TREE` but not `GIT_INDEX_FILE` which causes index corruption when:\n\n1. the user has added a plugin dep and quit neovim before installing it\n2. that user then runs `git --git-dir some-git-repo commit` with neovim as EDITOR\n3. on startup mini.deps runs git clone\n\ni think there are other environment variables which could have an effect too, like `GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY`. probably we want to remove all `GIT_` variables except for `GIT_SSH_COMMAND` and `GIT_ASKPASS`.\n\nexpected: installing a plugin shouldn't touch another repo.\n\n### Reproduction\n\ni added one line to the config in the template:\n\n```lua\nMiniDeps.add('gpanders/nvim-parinfer')\n```\n\nto reproduce git needs to be run with an explicit git-dir. bare dotfiles setups do this, e.g. `alias .f=\"git --git-dir=$HOME/.files\"`. that's how i hit it.\n\n```sh\nmkdir /tmp/bug && cd /tmp/bug\ngit init -q .\necho hi > file.txt\ngit add file.txt\ngit commit -m \"add file.txt\"\n```\n\nremove the plugin so mini.deps clones it on the next startup:\n\n```sh\nrm -rf ~/.local/share/nvim-repro/site/pack/deps/opt/nvim-parinfer\n```\n\namend with nvim-repro as EDITOR:\n\n```sh\nEDITOR='env NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim' git --git-dir=/tmp/bug/.git commit --amend\n```\n\nmini.deps installs nvim-parinfer while COMMIT_EDITMSG is open. `:wq`, amend succeeds:\n\n```\n[trunk 082f515] amended message\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\n```\n\nrepo is broken now:\n\n```\n$ git --git-dir=/tmp/bug/.git status\nfatal: unable to read 98b9384fdfed96bb116214532b445bfae9d89073\n```\n\nits index is nvim-parinfer's:\n\n```\n$ git --git-dir=/tmp/bug/.git ls-files\n.gitattributes\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nREADME.md\nautoload/parinfer.vim\ndoc/parinfer.txt\nfnl/parinfer/setup.fnl\nlua/parinfer.lua\nlua/parinfer/setup.lua\nplugin/parinfer.vim\n```\n\n```\n$ git --git-dir=/tmp/bug/.git fsck\nerror: c260b8ce7738d4fd536926fac0bb44ca7995e1e1: invalid sha1 pointer in cache-tree of /tmp/bug/.git/index\nmissing blob e20650813e0aa2b867f6925f3607df4418a361a2\nmissing blob 634a1425af16a57deda9c17a7597694b524c6203\n...\n```\n\nblobs are unreadable since mini.deps clones with `--filter=blob:none`. nvim-parinfer gets no index either:\n\n```\n$ ls ~/.local/share/nvim-repro/site/pack/deps/opt/nvim-parinfer/.git/index\nls: cannot access '...': No such file or directory\n```",
