        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue! This one deserves the \"one of the most niche and involved to reproduce\" award :)\n\nI did not try to reproduce, but I believe that this can happen. As an issue for 'mini.deps', I don't think it makes sense to fix for at least these reasons:\n- 'mini.deps' is now frozen in favor of `vim.pack`. I'd ask to see if this can be reproduced in `vim.pack` with the same severity and open an issue upstream. My initial reaction is that it will behave the same *but* there will be a confirmation dialog before faulty plugin installation. Pressing `n` should be enough to block the installation.\n- This looks like a *very* niche and *very* advanced use case that needs a lot of moving parts to reproduce. At this level, I'd assume that the user knows what they are doing and how to fix the problem (which seems to be true based on this issue).\n- I personally am not really fond of an idea to have an extensive blocklist of manually tracked environment variables that *might* cause issues in some edge cases. The current two variables already cause enough friction, adding more specially treated variables might lead to other edge cases. If there were some reasonable `git` flag(s) to achieve proper behavior, I'd maybe reconsider.\n\nSo all in all, I think closing this as not planned makes the most sense. Thanks for taking to create a detailed repro, though!",
